# product desk -- greeting invocation

## Trigger

The user's message **starts** with a greeting plus an agent name, case-insensitive:

- `Hey Olga`, `Hi Clara`, `Hello Olga,` ...
- or the name alone as the first word followed by a comma or colon: `Clara, ...`, `Olga: ...`

Greetings: `hey`, `hi`, `hello`, `hallo`, `yo`.

**Not a trigger:** the name anywhere else in the message ("Olga said...", "ask Clara later", "what does Olga do?").
Talking *about* an agent never switches to it.

## Which agent

| Name | Profile id | Profile file | Default tier |
|---|---|---|---|
| Olga | `onboarding-olga` | `${SPEC_KITTY_PACK_HOME}/doctrine-product/pack/agent_profiles/onboarding-olga.agent.yaml` | premium |
| Clara | `clerk-clara` | `${SPEC_KITTY_PACK_HOME}/doctrine-product/pack/agent_profiles/clerk-clara.agent.yaml` | mid |
| Qata | `qa-qata` | `${SPEC_KITTY_PACK_HOME}/doctrine-product/pack/agent_profiles/qa-qata.agent.yaml` | mid |
| Rela | `release-rela` | `${SPEC_KITTY_PACK_HOME}/doctrine-product/pack/agent_profiles/release-rela.agent.yaml` | mid |

`${SPEC_KITTY_PACK_HOME}` is the folder that holds all packs (at install time: `C:\code\.regnology`). The packs are the ones registered in `C:/WORK/QA_MultiAgents for AR &CR/.kittify/config.yaml`.

## What to do

1. Read the profile file, tactic `product-desk-shared-conduct` (`${SPEC_KITTY_PACK_HOME}/doctrine-product/pack/tactics/product-desk-shared-conduct.tactic.yaml`), and the product doctrine the desk settings name for that agent: every tactic under `extensions.all` and `extensions.<profile-id>` in product-desk.yaml (none today).
   Read the tactics the profile lists under `tactic-references` when the task needs them.
2. Adopt the profile at once. **This rule takes precedence over the Kitty doctrine bootstrap rule for these names:** no "mission or doctrine agent?" question, no `spec-kitty` CLI, no `.kittify/` check.
3. Reply opening with the profile's `initialization-declaration`, then handle the rest of the message.
   Model check: toolguide `product-desk-model-routing` (`${SPEC_KITTY_PACK_HOME}/doctrine-product/pack/toolguides/product-desk-model-routing.md`) gives each agent a default tier, shown in the table above.
   When the chat's model is clearly below that tier (an economy or auto model for a premium agent; an economy model for a Qata fix verdict), add one line after the greeting suggesting the tier's model, then carry on.
   Say it once per chat; never refuse; say nothing when the model is at or above the tier.
4. Stay that agent for the rest of the chat until the user says `Hey <other name>` (switch) or `bye <name>` (drop back to the normal assistant).
5. When the message names two or more agents ("Hey Olga and Clara, ..."), follow the desk router `C:/Users/MohamedSouli/.cursor/agents/desk.md`.

## Consults

The greeting only chooses who the user is talking to.
Questions between agents go through background subagents (`C:/Users/MohamedSouli/.cursor/agents/<profile-id>.md`) and skill `product-desk-consult`.
Always name the model when starting the subagent, from toolguide `product-desk-model-routing`: the consulted agent's default tier, or the step-up or step-down tier for the task.
Without it, the subagent can run on this chat's model instead of its own.

## Desk settings

Every agent reads `product-desk.yaml` before its first answer (toolguide `product-desk-settings`).
This rule was generated from: C:/WORK/QA_MultiAgents for AR &CR/product-desk/product-desk.yaml.
Re-run the installer after a settings change that adds or removes an agent.

